.Sh DESCRIPTION
SHA-2 (Secure Hash Algorithm 2) is a family of cryptographic hash
functions standardized in NIST FIPS 180-4, first published in 2001.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_sha224(), EVP_sha256(), EVP_sha512_224, EVP_sha512_256, EVP_sha384(), EVP_sha512()
The SHA-2 SHA-224, SHA-256, SHA-512/224, SHA512/256, SHA-384 and SHA-512
algorithms, which generate 224, 256, 224, 256, 384 and 512 bits
respectively of output from a given input.
.Pp
The two algorithms: SHA-512/224 and SHA512/256 are truncated forms of
the SHA-512 algorithm.
They are distinct from SHA-224 and SHA-256 even though their outputs are
of the same size.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Developers should be aware of the negative performance implications of
calling these functions multiple times and should consider using
.Xr EVP_MD_fetch 3
with
.Xr EVP_MD-SHA2 7 Ns instead.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return a
.Sy EVP_MD
structure that contains the implementation of the message digest.
See
.Xr EVP_MD_meth_new 3
for details of the
.Sy EVP_MD
structure.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
NIST FIPS 180-4.
